From 27028e5733fa6b6342ebb627a13be5974d9040bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:57:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban CI progress: a job-read error no longer ends
 the pool scan before a later batch's match (#2321 review)

With the runner lists unreadable, `_recent_job_on` scans every in-progress
run's jobs (POOL_SCAN_READERS at a time), then recently completed runs, for a
job a runner took on the queued run's labels. `batch()` raised its first
job-read error when its own batch had no match, and the outer `except`
returned "". So one 502 on one run's jobs in an early batch stopped the whole
scan: a matching job in a later batch (or in the completed-runs list) was
never read, and the card read `not_starting` -- the false runners-offline wake
#2235/#2321 exist to prevent.

Fix: a failed job read (or run-list read) is noted and the scan goes on
through the remaining batches and the completed-runs list. The first match
wins and is remembered as before. Only when nothing matched and some read
failed is "" returned without caching it, so an unreadable scan is still not
remembered. OverBudget/deadline handling is unchanged; an unexpected
(non-I/O) exception still propagates.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ci_progress.py
- test_unreadable_job_list_in_an_earlier_batch_does_not_end_the_scan[match]:
  10 runs, 502 on run 901 (batch 1), running job on LABELS in run 908
  (batch 2) -> BUSY and remembered. RED before (not_starting).
- ...[no-match]: same error, no match -> NOT_STARTING, run 908 still read,
  not remembered. RED before (908 never read).
- test_unreadable_job_list_does_not_skip_the_completed_runs: 502 on the only
  in-progress run, match in a recent completed run -> BUSY. RED before.
Full file: 73 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.

Follow-up of review 5893630788 on #2321 (card t_01a1d580f60a9779).
